---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import LegalNotice from '../components/LegalNotice.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_LINKS } from '../consts'
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — RealtyBase" noindex>
	<SiteHeader />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
		<h1 class="text-foreground mb-6 text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Terms of Service</h1>

		<LegalNotice />

		<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
			Effective date: to be confirmed upon legal review.
		</p>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">1. Introduction / Acceptance of Terms</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				These Terms of Service govern access to and use of the RealtyBase platform, operated by RealtyBase Inc.
				("RealtyBase," "we," "us," or "our"). By creating an account or otherwise using the Service, a Brokerage
				and its authorized users agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, you should not use the
				Service.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">2. Definitions</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				"Service" means the RealtyBase platform and its associated web and application interfaces. "Account"
				means the credentials and profile used to access the Service. "Brokerage" means the real estate
				brokerage entity that maintains an account. "User" means any individual accessing the Service under a
				Brokerage's account. "Content" means listings, documents, comments, and other material submitted to the
				Service.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">3. Eligibility / Account Registration</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				Accounts are registered by a Brokerage's owners or administrators, who are responsible for the accuracy
				of the information provided during registration and for the conduct of Users they invite. A Brokerage
				must keep its account information current and promptly update it if it changes.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">4. Description of Service</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				RealtyBase provides a workspace for real estate brokerages to manage listings, organize staff and
				clients into groups, and collaborate on shared content. The Service is provided on an evolving basis,
				and features may be added, changed, or removed over time.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">5. Subscription Plans and Billing</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				Access to the Service is subject to plans and fees as described at the time of purchase. Plan details,
				including current offerings and fees, are made available through the Service itself rather than in
				these Terms, so that this document does not go out of date as offerings change. A Brokerage is
				responsible for the charges associated with the plan it selects.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">6. User Responsibilities / Acceptable Use</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				Users must not misuse the Service, attempt to access accounts or data they are not authorized to
				access, or interfere with the Service's normal operation. Users are responsible for the accuracy of
				listings and other Content they submit and for complying with applicable real estate laws and board
				rules that apply to their own activities.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">7. Intellectual Property</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				RealtyBase retains all rights to the Service itself, including its software, design, and branding. A
				Brokerage and its Users retain ownership of the Content they submit, such as listings and documents, and
				grant RealtyBase only the rights needed to operate and provide the Service on their behalf.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">8. Data Ownership and Privacy</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				Data submitted to the Service remains the property of the Brokerage that submitted it. How RealtyBase
				collects, uses, and protects information in connection with the Service is described in the
				<a href={LEGAL_LINKS.privacy} class="text-primary underline-offset-2 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>,
				which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">9. Termination</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				A Brokerage may stop using the Service at any time. RealtyBase may suspend or terminate access to the
				Service if these Terms are violated or if continued access would create a legal or security risk. Upon
				termination, provisions of these Terms that by their nature should survive will continue to apply.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">10. Disclaimers and Limitation of Liability</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				The Service is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, to the extent
				permitted by law. RealtyBase's liability for any claim arising out of the Service will be limited as
				described here once this section has been reviewed and finalized by legal counsel.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">11. Indemnification</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				A Brokerage agrees to indemnify and hold RealtyBase harmless from claims arising out of its, or its
				Users', misuse of the Service or violation of these Terms, to the extent permitted by law. The specific
				scope of this obligation is pending confirmation by legal counsel.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">12. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				The governing jurisdiction and dispute resolution process for these Terms are pending confirmation by
				legal counsel and will be specified here once finalized, rather than assumed in advance.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">13. Changes to Terms</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We may update these Terms from time to time. If we make material changes, we will update the effective
				date above and, where appropriate, provide additional notice to account holders.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">14. Contact Us</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				If you have questions about these Terms, contact us at
				<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
